      "content": "The dipole of CCl<sub>4</sub>, CHCl<sub>3</sub> and CH<sub>4</sub> are in the order :",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "CCl<sub>4</sub> &lt; CH<sub>4</sub> &lt; CHCl<sub>3</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "CH<sub>4</sub> = CCl<sub>4</sub> &lt; CHCl<sub>3</sub>\n"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "CH<sub>4</sub> &lt; CCl<sub>4</sub> &lt; CHCl<sub>3</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "CHCl<sub>3</sub> &lt; CH<sub>4</sub>= CCl<sub>4</sub>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "B"
      ],
      "explanation": "CHCl<sub>3</sub> is polar while CH<sub>4</sub> and CCl<sub>4</sub> are nonpolar.\n<br><br>So, dipole moment order is :\n<br><br> CH<sub>4</sub> = CCl<sub>4</sub> &lt; CHCl<sub>3</sub>\n"
    }
